<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21368" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭdūmaea</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰδουμαία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a region of
			Palestine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 14, 15, §
			70</span></i>.—Called also <b>poet.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭdūmē</span></b> , es,
				f., <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 1, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			216</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭdūmaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Idumea</i>, <i>Idumean;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> also for <i>Palestinian</i>, <i>Jewish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palmae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triumphi,</span>”
				<i>over Judea</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 160</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
